.TH RSTORY 6.SH NAMErstory \- tell a cumulative tale at random.SH SYNOPSIS\fBrstory\fR.SH DESCRIPTION\fBrstory\fRtells a story in the shape of\fIThe Old Woman and Her Pig\fR:\fRsomeone goes to market, buys an animal that will not cross an obstacleon the way home, and asks one helper after another -- a scissor to snipthe dog, a girl to break the scissor -- each refusal adding a line tothe chain until the last one gives in.  Who, what and every helper arechosen at random, so no two runs are alike..PPIt writes one long paragraph;\fBtformat\fRsets it justified under a heading with the date:\fBrstory | tformat\fR(or\fBrstory ! tformat\fRat Microware's shell)..SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/RSTORY.SYN\fR.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/RSTORY.ACT\fRthe characters, the obstacles and what each helper does..SH NOTESOne of Robert Heller's programs translated from SNOBOL4 into C, fromJames F. Gimpel's\fIAlgorithms in SNOBOL4\fR;\fR\fBDOC/snobol\fRdescribes the set and\fBSRC/effo_snobol\fRholds the source..SH SEE ALSOtformat, rpoem